\begin{definition}[Moderately hard function]
Let $d_0, d_1$ be polynomials, let $\beta : \mathbb{N} \times \mathbb{N} \to (0,1]$ and $\epsilon : \mathbb{N} \times \mathbb{N} \to [0,1]$ be functions, and let $(\mathsf{Gen}, f)$ be a challenge sampler together with a function family as above, with evaluation cost $r(s,\lambda)$. We say $(\mathsf{Gen}, f)$ is \emph{$(d_0,d_1,\beta,\epsilon)$-moderately hard} if for every $t \le d_0(\lambda)$ and every pair of PPT algorithms $\mathcal{A} = (\mathcal{A}_0, \mathcal{A}_1)$ such that $\mathcal{A}_1$ runs in at most $t \cdot \beta(s,\lambda) \cdot r(s,\lambda)$ steps and makes at most $d_1(\lambda)$ queries to $\mathcal{O}_f$, none of which lies in $\{z_1,\dots,z_t\}$, it holds for all sufficiently large $\lambda, s \in \mathbb{N}$ that
\[
\Pr\!\left[\, \forall h \in [t] : w_h = f_{s,\lambda}(z_h) \;\middle|\;
\begin{array}{l}
\mathsf{aux} \leftarrow \mathcal{A}_0(1^{\lambda},1^{s}) \\
z_1,\dots,z_{d_0(\lambda)} \leftarrow \mathsf{Gen}(1^{\lambda}) \ \text{i.i.d.} \\
(w_h)_{h \in [t]} \leftarrow \mathcal{A}_1^{\mathcal{O}_f}\!\big(1^{\lambda},1^{s},(z_h)_{h \in [d_0(\lambda)]},\mathsf{aux}\big)
\end{array}
\right] \;\le\; \epsilon(t,\lambda).
\]
(The adversary is handed $d_0(\lambda)$ challenges but is only required to solve the first $t$ of them. The restriction that the oracle is not queried on $z_1,\dots,z_t$ is what makes the notion non-trivial when $d_1 \ge t$.)
\end{definition}

\begin{definition}[NSETH]
For every $\varepsilon > 0$ there exists $k \in \mathbb{N}$ such that $k$-$\mathsf{TAUT}$ --- the problem of deciding whether a given $k$-DNF formula on $N$ variables is a tautology --- cannot be decided by a nondeterministic algorithm running in time $O(2^{(1-\varepsilon)N})$.
\end{definition}
